{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0097594","isObsolete":false,"name":"ventral disc dorsal microribbon","definition":{"text":"Trilaminar structure extending perpendicularly into the cytoplasm along the length of ventral disc microtubules in Giardia species (trophozoite stage). Constituents of dorsal microribbons (also called dorsal ribbons or microribbons) include alpha-coiled-helix proteins approximately 29 to 38 kDa in size. These proteins line the edges of the microribbons but are not found in microtubules. Tubulins are not found in microribbons.","xrefs":[{"dbCode":"PMID","dbId":"11432808"}]},"comment":"Due to the asymmetric nature of the Giardia trophozoite, this term is defined spatially as the trophozoite is viewed from the dorsal side, with the two nuclei dorsal to the ventral disc, and the ventral disc toward the anterior.","synonyms":[{"name":"dorsal microribbon","type":"broad"},{"name":"dorsal ribbon","type":"broad"},{"name":"microribbon","type":"broad"},{"name":"ventral disk dorsal microribbon","type":"related"}],"history":[{"timestamp":"2024-03-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2019-09-12","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0110165 (cellular anatomical structure)"},{"timestamp":"2019-09-12","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044422 (obsolete organelle part)"},{"timestamp":"2018-08-18","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"part of GO:0097597 (ventral disc)"},{"timestamp":"2014-04-06","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"has part GO:0097597 (ventral disc)"},{"timestamp":"2014-04-06","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044422 (obsolete organelle part)"},{"timestamp":"2014-04-06","action":"Added","category":"TERM","text":"ventral disc dorsal microribbon"},{"timestamp":"2014-04-06","action":"Added","category":"SYNONYM","text":"ventral disk dorsal microribbon"},{"timestamp":"2014-04-06","action":"Added","category":"SYNONYM","text":"dorsal microribbon"},{"timestamp":"2014-04-06","action":"Added","category":"SYNONYM","text":"dorsal ribbon"},{"timestamp":"2014-04-06","action":"Added","category":"SYNONYM","text":"microribbon"},{"timestamp":"2014-04-06","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"Trilaminar structure extending perpendicularly into the cytoplasm along the length of ventral disc microtubules in Giardia species (trophozoite stage). Constituents of dorsal microribbons (also called dorsal ribbons or microribbons) include alpha-coiled-helix proteins approximately 29 to 38 kDa in size. These proteins line the edges of the microribbons but are not found in microtubules. Tubulins are not found in microribbons."}],"taxonConstraints":[{"ancestorId":"GO:0097594","ancestorName":"ventral disc dorsal microribbon","relationship":"only_in_taxon","taxId":"5740","taxIdType":"NCBITaxon","taxName":"Giardia"}],"aspect":"cellular_component","usage":"Unrestricted","blacklist":[{"goId":"GO:0097594","reason":"1 NOT-qualified manual annotation exists with evidence code ECO:0000314 from this reference: PMID:22247266","category":"NOT-qualified manual","entityType":"protein","entityId":"A8BER9","taxonId":"184922","entityName":"MEDB_GIAIC","ancestorGoId":"GO:0097594"},{"goId":"GO:0097594","reason":"1 NOT-qualified manual annotation exists with evidence code ECO:0000314 from this reference: PMID:17766466","category":"NOT-qualified manual","entityType":"protein","entityId":"E2RU10","taxonId":"184922","entityName":"EB1_GIAIC","ancestorGoId":"GO:0097597"},{"goId":"GO:0097594","reason":"1 NOT-qualified manual annotation exists with evidence code ECO:0000250 from this reference: GO_REF:0000024","category":"NOT-qualified manual","entityType":"protein","entityId":"Q08014","taxonId":"5741","entityName":"MEDB_GIAIN","ancestorGoId":"GO:0097594"}]}],"pageInfo":null}